think Standfast on reds: read crux/REDS.md whole. Every living row is Closed, Released, or the custody-gated errata #75 (a history rewrite that stays Keaton's hand, not a code red). Standfast clear -- no open agent-closable red blocks new work.
think The named crux: connectivity_threshold gave the bottleneck VALUE (one number, the largest MST edge); the MST names the actual bridge EDGES -- which cluster pair bridges which -- so a surface can DRAW the skeleton, not only know at what reach it closes. Lindy-first (a relational scene primitive read for years), crux-first (the hardest-solvable move that opens the rest, lifting a number to an edge set).
think Read the two closest modules (cluster_connectivity.rye, cluster_graph.rye) to match shape exactly -- the union-find, the local canvas builders, the graph_of helper, the two proven scenes. Built image/cluster_minimum_spanning_tree.rye: build_mst grows the tree by Prim over cluster_graph's precomputed matrix (start cluster 1, attach the nearest not-yet-in-tree cluster, ties to the lowest id for determinism), mst_weight, mst_bottleneck, edge_count, is_bridge.
think Crux shape ONE -- THE MST IS THE SKELETON, ITS BOTTLENECK THE CONNECTIVITY THRESHOLD: over the three-cluster scene (distances 2, 3, 10) the tree picks edges 1-2 (gap 2) and 1-3 (gap 3) and never the diameter edge 2-3 (gap 10), a STAR on the hub cluster 1; its bottleneck (3) EQUALS cluster_connectivity.connectivity_threshold (cross-checked, never re-derived), yet the tree also names WHICH two edges close the layout where the threshold named only the value; weight 5 far below the pairwise sum 15, the diameter edge never spent because the hub bridges the far pair for less.
think Crux shape TWO -- THE TREE DROPS THE REDUNDANT CYCLE EDGE, FEWER EDGES THAN THE THRESHOLDED GRAPH: over a four-cluster scene (a triangle mutually 3 apart plus a far outlier 9 away) the thresholded graph at reach 3 holds three edges (the whole triangle, a cycle), yet the MST over four clusters holds exactly n-1 = 3 edges (two triangle edges plus the one bridge to the outlier); the third triangle edge 2-3 is DROPPED though its gap 3 is within the tree's bottleneck 9 and sits in the thresholded graph, because a spanning tree carries no cycle -- is_bridge(2,3) reads FALSE for an edge the connectivity read would have counted. The bottleneck (9) still equals the connectivity threshold: the skeleton and the threshold meet at the largest edge and part on every other.
think Prim's from cluster 1 over the four-cluster scene yields a STAR (edges 1-2, 1-3, 1-4) since the hub's ties are broken by lowest id, so the dropped cycle edge is 2-3 -- exactly the shape that makes the crux plain. Verified geometry: triangle blocks mutually Chebyshev 3, outlier 9 from each, matching cluster_connectivity's own scene two.
